WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.590
What is that thing?

2
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.680
-We gotta get outta here!
-Wait! It might attack if we move!

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.260
-Then what do we do?
-There has to be a way to escape!

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.930
-Don't expect me to find it!
-Two of us just died!

5
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.610
Everyone. stay still!
I think moving makes it mad too!

6
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.490
Hey. hey. Joohee! Stay with me!

7
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.660
That was a close one.

8
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.700
We'd all be piles of ash right now

9
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.370
-if it weren't for you. kid.
-Me?

10
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.630
You yelled because
you figured it out. right?

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.170
No. sir. It was because I
sensed something dangerous.

12
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.290
Mister Song! Your arm!

13
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.550
If I grit my teeth.
it isn't all that bad.

14
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.640
But could you stop
the bleeding for me?

15
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.260
Normally. I'd ask the party's
healer to patch me up.

16
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.610
Ours spooks easily. though.

17
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:59.150
That's why she only does bottom rung
raids despite being a B-Rank hunter.

18
00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:03.900
I've raided B-Rank dungeons and lived
to tell the tale a couple of times myself.

19
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.280
Something that insta-kills
has to be an A-Rank.

20
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.950
If not S.

21
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.410
Those three commandments of the
Cartenon Temple aren't there for fun.

22
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.540
"First. thou shalt worship God."

23
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.750
"Second. thou shalt praise God."

24
00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.000
"Third. thou shalt prove thy faith."

25
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.710
"Those who do not follow these
laws will not leave alive."

26
00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.800
Hold on.

27
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.010
So when it says. "God."

28
00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.140
it's talking about that thing?

29
00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.470
When the first gate appeared.

30
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:36.770
it gave rise to a number of
supernatural phenomena.

31
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.480
The likes of which humanity could
only fathom in their wildest dreams.

32
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.700
Those who awakened as hunters are
a prime example of one such wonder.

33
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.660
They used their enhanced
abilities to conquer the beasts

34
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.450
lurking in the dungeons
beyond the gates.

35
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.460
Though their power is static
from the moment it sparks to life.

36
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:03.290
To call a hunter "courageous"
would be an understatement.

37
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:07.380
For the terrors they find don't
merely strike fear in their hearts.

38
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.020
But can leave them in utter despair.

39
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.810
-Did you see?
-Oh. that video clip?

40
00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.940
Cuttin' it real close. Y'wanna
share what almost made you late?

41
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.320
Yeah. no.

42
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.700
Hm.

43
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.540
Hey. your brother awakened
as a hunter. right. Jinah?

44
00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.330
He did. The powers he got only
scored him an E-Rank. though.

45
00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.990
so he does tend to come home
with more wounds than treasure.

46
00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.270
Looked like a regular
mummy the other day!

47
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.670
But. why randomly ask about that?

48
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.220
No reason.

49
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.690
If I was a hunter.
I'd make E-rank look good.

50
00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.100
It's too strong to fight.

51
00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.310
Meaning our objective
now is to escape.

52
00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.810
-Let's collect ourselves--
-I'm not dying in here!

53
00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:24.310
No. I just landed a
contract with a major guild!

54
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.110
Got too much going for me
to bite it in this crap hole!

55
00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.110
If that's true. then don't move!

56
00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.820
I can do this!
Speed's my specialty!

57
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.240
I'll get outta here. watch me!

58
00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.880
Damn it!

59
00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:51.420
That thing can end us
the second it feels like it.

60
00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:55.520
Yeah. we're basically bugs
waiting to be vaporized.

61
00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:59.890
Then. do you have any idea
why it hasn't zapped us all yet?

62
00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:00.970
No.

63
00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.640
So it could kill us. but it's not.

64
00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.280
What's weirder is any other
magic beast would attack on sight.

65
00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.980
The writing! What'd the first
commandment say again?

66
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.780
What?
Oh. the very first one was...

67
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.870
"Thou shall worship God."

68
00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.160
God.

69
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.530
This place has its own rules.

70
00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.250
What the heck are you doing?

71
00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.290
Testing a theory.

72
00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.960
Sit down. or...

73
00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.460
You aren't done.

74
00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.310
That isn't the look of a man
who's given up yet.

75
00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.490
We need to bow our heads
toward the giant statue on the throne!

76
00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.240
Will that actually do something?

77
00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.990
I think you might have snapped. kid.

78
00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.860
-So your theory was right then?
-Yes. sir.

79
00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.780
It only attacks if you're
above a certain height.

80
00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:08.170
We have to bow down and "worship
God" like the commandment says.

81
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.050
This is your plan
to get us out of here?

82
00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:17.060
Yes. For now.

83
00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.430
Guess it's worth a shot.

84
00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.450
A little courtesy?
That's what's gonna save us?

85
00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.280
Damn. that's freaky!

86
00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.530
Its face. It changed?

87
00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.870
It isn't doing anything.

88
00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.170
Beom-shik!
Why are you standing?

89
00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.410
You see? I'm still okay!

90
00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.920
It worked.

91
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.130
So that really was all it took.

92
00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.630
-No more lasers?
-Good riddance!

93
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.130
-We made it!
-We can go home!

94
00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.140
No. not quite.

95
00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.060
I thought this nightmare was over!

96
00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.570
C'mon. Jinwoo. what's next?
Does your plan have a second phase?

97
00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.570
Well. not really. no.

98
00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.950
But if we keep obeying those commandments.
I have a hunch we'll be all right.

99
00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.660
Meaning the next step
should be to praise God!

100
00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.450
-Praise the giant?
-How exactly?

101
00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.750
I might have the answer.

102
00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.460
As a dedicated student of ethnology.
I have a few extolments for Gods

103
00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.590
tucked away in the back of my mind.

104
00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:45.380
O mighty Lord. Praise be to you
who brings order to the world...

105
00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.180
I can't tell if it's working.

106
00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.810
Looks like it's slowing
down. so maybe?

107
00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.350
Show us the righteous path of truth.

108
00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.350
That prayer. Wait.

109
00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.940
Thy will be done. O Lord.
for only you know the way.

110
00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.240
No! It doesn't apply to this God!

111
00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.860
We revere and honor your holy name!

112
00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.330
O wondrous ruler. hear my cries!

113
00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.080
For it's in your name I--

114
00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:15.930
-Shit!
-Let's move!

115
00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.740
Everyone. spread out till
we come up with something.

116
00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.640
Take my hand!

117
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.760
No way I'm dying like this.

118
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.860
I've got a family waiting for me.

119
00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.520
I think the safest place
is up against the walls.

120
00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.950
No. Beom-shik!
Look behind you!

121
00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.210
Beom-shik!

122
00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.470
Praise God. Praise God.

123
00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.170
What is there to
praise about that thing?

124
00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.260
It's more demonic than divine.

125
00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.770
Whatever I do. I'm not
leaving Joohee by herself.

126
00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.220
What's the hint here?

127
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.640
Spear. axe.

128
00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.280
It's all a bad dream.
I'll wake up an--

129
00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.770
Hammer. sword.

130
00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.650
Trumpet.

131
00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.980
Trumpet! That's it!

132
00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.120
I got it.

133
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.570
Everyone. quick!

134
00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.410
Run to the statues
holding musical instruments!

135
00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:32.200
If you say so.

136
00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.290
What do you know?
Kid was right again.

137
00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:43.760
Hey. none of the statues with instruments
will attack. so hurry and find one.

138
00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.520
Damn it all.

139
00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.770
Come on. play your drum!
Come on. please!

140
00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.940
Is it just one person per statue?

141
00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.310
Stay here. You'll be fine.

142
00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.860
What about you?

143
00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.580
So close!

144
00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.250
Not that one!

145
00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.220
No!

146
00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.600
Please don't die!

147
00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.890
Not yet.

148
00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.830
Not yet.

149
00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.700
Not yet.

150
00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:14.010
Feel like singing praises myself.

151
00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.020
Jinwoo! Are you okay?

152
00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.070
Barely. but at least I'm alive.

153
00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.320
Oh. my gosh.

154
00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.700
What's wrong?

155
00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.210
Oh.

156
00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:39.540
Your leg.

157
00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.210
Enough already. I mean it.

158
00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.920
You'll wear yourself
out if you don't stop.

159
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.380
I'm going to heal you!

160
00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.510
So just shut up and let me do it!

161
00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.690
I'm sorry. Joohee.

162
00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:59.100
What a bloodbath.

163
00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.520
No kidding.

164
00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.810
I count your arm as a casualty. too.

165
00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.730
But I also count it as
karma since you led us here.

166
00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.620
-Nice call. by the way.
-That's awful.

167
00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.280
You're the one who said
we should bend the rules...

168
00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.150
I did what we all decided on!

169
00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.320
And I remember how you voted.

170
00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.040
Sangshik is right.

171
00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.700
I'm the leader
and I had the final say.

172
00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.290
I'm the one to blame for everything.

173
00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.410
It's no time to point fingers.

174
00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:25.330
There's one more trial left.

175
00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.500
What's happening now?

176
00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.180
Earthquake?

177
00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.090
The hell is that?

178
00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.480
An altar.

179
00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:40.720
You know. like the kind
in ancient mythology.

180
00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.510
For offerings to the Gods
they pray to.

181
00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.550
Proving our faith
is the last commandment.

182
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:51.730
I may not be the smartest. but
even I know what move to make.

183
00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:57.210
This God likes blood. so it's fair to
assume that it wants a sacrifice!

184
00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.660
Beom-shik had a family.

185
00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.160
Bragged about it all day. then
I watched him get cut in half.

186
00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.000
He and six others died.

187
00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:11.420
If you really feel responsible for their
deaths. prove it to us and God. leader.

188
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.050
-No. Mister Kim. that's...
-You stay out of this!

189
00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:16.850
All right.

190
00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:19.060
Lower your sword and I'll go.

191
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.300
He shouldn't shoulder all the blame.

192
00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.780
We voted as a group
to risk coming here.

193
00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:31.570
So is the ritual beginning?

194
00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.240
Hm. Hey. kid. what do you think?

195
00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.780
Am I supposed to do
something with this flame?

196
00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:43.120
I'm not sure. but.
maybe a sacrifice isn't the key.

197
00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:45.790
Hey. if you wouldn't mind.

198
00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:49.010
Could you two carry me?
I wanna check something.

199
00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:53.880
Just get me right
next to the altar. okay?

200
00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.510
But won't we all die?

201
00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:57.560
Hypothetically. we shouldn't.

202
00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.940
Did you solve the last puzzle?

203
00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.810
Sorry. not quite.

204
00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:12.230
If we wait here. is anyone
likely to come rescue us?

205
00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.190
Today marks the seventh day
this gate's been open.

206
00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.740
Those statues will mobilize
again before a rescue team does.

207
00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.700
It takes a week for a gate
to open all the way.

208
00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:30.630
And then. the beasts inside
can cross over.

209
00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:32.960
A dungeon break.

210
00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:37.300
The other objective of
raids. besides scavenging.

211
00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:41.680
is to beat the dungeon boss and
shut the gate down before time's up.

212
00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:44.220
So. if the six of us fail.

213
00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.940
that thing will be let loose.

214
00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:51.480
-Good afternoon!
-And same to you. Miss Sung.

215
00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.400
Always nice to see your face.

216
00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:02.360
Hey. Mom!
It's your favorite daughter.

217
00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:06.120
Only hot gossip I have to spill
is that Song-yi was almost late.

218
00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.580
Said it was 'cause of "stuff."

219
00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:10.170
Bet she just slept in.

220
00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.840
I've also got a national test update.

221
00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:20.130
You're going to have to get
near the altar. too.

222
00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:23.260
We probably need a flame
to light up for each of us.

223
00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.720
If anything happens.
it'll be after that.

224
00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:27.860
Hm.

225
00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.570
-The doors opened.
-So can we leave?

226
00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.500
That's bait if I ever saw it.

227
00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.290
That doesn't sound good.

228
00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.040
Look! The statues are closing in!

229
00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.590
Do we have a plan?

230
00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:59.180
What in their psycho
God's name do they want?

231
00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.130
Why?

232
00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.350
Wait. Joohee!
Don't close your eyes!

233
00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:08.940
Or they'll keep coming.

234
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:12.220
See? Look. just like
that old kid's game.

235
00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.400
So. all eyes on the statues!

236
00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.000
Wait. don't go!

237
00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.420
Talk to us. kid!
Now what's going on?

238
00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.590
The doors closed a little.
but I think she made it out!

239
00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:41.300
Why? Okay.

240
00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.000
The blue flames have been
slowly dying out one by one.

241
00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.810
and the red flames go out
when we leave the circle?

242
00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:47.970
Think.

243
00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.810
First we had to worship.

244
00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:52.100
Second. we have to praise.

245
00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.600
Then now. we prove our faith.

246
00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:57.860
The open doors are a trap.

247
00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.440
Offering false hope
in the wake of terror.

248
00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.270
Maybe we prove our faith by
resisting the temptation to run.

249
00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:05.910
Guys. I can't.

250
00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.620
I tried. but I can't.

251
00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.750
Jeongho. don't!

252
00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:14.710
No!

253
00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:20.290
-Hey! Huh?
-Don't you dare move!

254
00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:23.500
The circle will have blind
spots if we lose our fourth!

255
00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.010
It'd be comforting if we had a
little more info to go on. here!

256
00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:30.970
We'll escape. too. if we keep our
eyes on the statues and stay put.

257
00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.890
The blue flames are a timer.

258
00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.350
When they're gone.
we can walk right out of here.

259
00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:40.060
There's also a chance the
doors will shut completely.

260
00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.940
And we'll be trapped
inside this room till we die.

261
00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:47.200
I never expected the weakest
hunter of all mankind to be

262
00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:49.450
the difference
between us living or dying.

263
00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:53.620
But I can honestly say that I've
never been happier to stand corrected.

264
00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.540
Oh. uh. thank you.

265
00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:59.580
But that said. I've got
a family that needs me.

266
00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.960
So dying in here
just isn't an option.

267
00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.330
I want to make it home alive.

268
00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.010
I'm way past my limit.

269
00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.850
I'm sorry.

270
00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.390
You're "sorry?"

271
00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:19.560
Not yet. We have to survive this.

272
00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.650
Somehow.

273
00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:23.610
I always pull through
every single time.

274
00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:29.700
You two go while you still can.

275
00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:31.530
Mister Song.

276
00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.950
I'll stay behind.

277
00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:36.830
As long as one of us waits in
here the doors should remain open.

278
00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:39.710
You both have so much life left
ahead of you. go and live it.

279
00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.080
So. Joohee.
Can you carry him out?

280
00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.670
S-Sure!

281
00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.680
No. No. no. no. no.

282
00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:52.140
Um. sir? My legs
just gave out on me.

283
00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:56.060
You really did overdo it
healing Jinwoo.

284
00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:59.140
You go. Take Joohee and leave.

285
00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.100
What? Did you even
listen to anything I said--

286
00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.690
You think I can carry her
with half a leg missing?

287
00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.280
We're wasting time! Just go!

288
00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.610
That makes me the useless one.
so I'll keep the doors open!

289
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.610
Guess I promised to take
you out to eat. now didn't I?

290
00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.580
Use this to buy yourself dinner.

291
00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.210
Once I make my grand escape.
I'll come collect the change.

292
00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.710
How're you cracking jokes right no--

293
00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:25.760
I apologize. I'd let you have a proper
goodbye. but we really are out of time.

294
00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.300
-Please take good care of her.
-I will.

295
00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:38.060
I'm glad my death means they can live.

296
00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.600
My one regret. though.

297
00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:44.270
is that I didn't enroll in a
juicier life insurance package.

298
00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:52.700
I'll take at least one of
you goliaths down with me!

299
00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.240
Let's see what you've got!

300
00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.340
I've always been the weakest.

301
00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:12.050
and I've been mocked
for it at every turn.

302
00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:15.180
But I still try as hard as I can.

303
00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:20.220
So this...

304
00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:22.520
Shit. Shit!

305
00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.770
This is bullshit.

306
00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:26.160
Bullshit!

307
00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.860
I wanted to be stronger.

308
00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.120
I tried. but...

309
00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.910
I never could.

310
00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:42.750
I get it! I fought tooth and nail to
earn my keep. and I got this far!

311
00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.340
But you were past your limit. huh?

312
00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.130
Yeah. we all felt that way.

313
00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:56.100
You were making excuses
for your own selfishness.

314
00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.970
That gratitude
was as empty as my wallet.

315
00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:03.140
Leave it to a genuine piece of trash.

316
00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:06.150
to use me and throw
me away for his benefit!

317
00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:08.020
I've got a family too!

318
00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.530
I wanted to make it home alive. too!

319
00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.290
I'm glad my death
means they can live?

320
00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:30.720
How could you think that.
you stupid hypocrite?

321
00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:36.980
No. I don't want to die.

322
00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.640
I wish...

323
00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:47.860
I had another chance.
